# Walking on the beach in Russian: гуляя, прилетев
subtitle: "Make Russian gerunds yourself on a Baltic beach: гуля́ют becomes гуля́я, прилете́л becomes прилете́в, and не зна́я."
tags: ["russian","russian gerunds","baltic sea","kaliningrad","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/gerunds","vocabulary/nature","vocabulary/travel"]
thumb: "band \"Walking on the beach, in one word\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Nobody to ask in Russian: некого, некогда, нечего","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/159-russian-nothing-to-do.cast"}

